  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-intelligent-ui",
      "text": "Interactive cards in DeepSeek Harness chats. The model writes a small interface program, the chat draws it as a native card, and every control recomputes in your browser without another model call. A button sends its text as your next message.\n\n[中文](README-zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-intelligent-ui",
      "text": "| | |\n|---|---|\n| Requires | DeepSeek Harness **>= 0.2.1-rc.1** (below 0.3.0) |\n| Platforms | Web UI, macOS desktop app, and Windows desktop app — one bundle, because both desktop apps load the same web client |\n| Verified | Web UI 0.2.1-alpha.4; macOS and Windows desktop apps 0.2.1-rc.2 |\n| Install | Settings → Plugins → Add plugin → `https://github.com/StarsHarryZhu/dsh-intelligent-UI` (needs `git` on `PATH`), then restart the harness and reload the page |"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "- The plugin registers one tool, `ui_render`, and one skill, `dsh-intelligent-ui`, which teaches the model when a card beats prose. The skill is its own part of the plugin: the Plugin Manager lists it with its own switch, and installing the plugin installs it. The model never writes HTML or JavaScript: its program is checked against the 35-component catalog and stored with the tool result. SVG it writes for a drawing is read into a checked tree with no scripts, styles, links, or images.\n- A card draws in the tool row while the reply streams, and under the reply once it finishes. Moving a control recomputes every figure locally, and this browser keeps what you set, so a reload shows the card as you left it.\n- Asked to change a card, the model draws a revised one that starts from your settings; the earlier card says a newer version follows.\n- A `player` animates a card: code traced line by line, an algorithm's passes, a point moving along a curve. With `loop=true autoplay=true` a drawing plays by itself while it is on screen, like a GIF: a rolling wheel, a travelling wave, an orbit. Playback runs in the browser and sends nothing to the model, and nothing starts by itself if your syst"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnode scripts/link-dev.mjs   # link the toolchain from the sibling harness checkout\nnode build.js               # type-check, build, and self-check the bundle\nnode node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run\n```\n\n`AGENTS.md` holds the rules of the tree; `docs/VERIFY.md` is the live checklist."
    },
    {
      "section": "The 35 components",
      "text": "One card per component, drawn by this plugin in the host's light theme. The program behind each card is in [`docs/SAMPLES.md`](docs/SAMPLES.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "`card` — Layout",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/card.png\" alt=\"card\" width=\"720\">\n\nThe framed root: optional title, padding, and gap."
    },
    {
      "section": "`col` — Layout",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/col.png\" alt=\"col\" width=\"720\">\n\nA vertical stack in reading order."
    },
    {
      "section": "`row` — Layout",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/row.png\" alt=\"row\" width=\"720\">\n\nEqual-width cells side by side; they wrap on a narrow screen."
    },
    {
      "section": "`grid` — Layout",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/grid.png\" alt=\"grid\" width=\"720\">\n\nAn even grid of one to four columns."
    },
    {
      "section": "`tabs` — Layout",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/tabs.png\" alt=\"tabs\" width=\"720\">\n\nPages the reader switches between, by click or arrow key; only the open page is drawn."
    },
    {
      "section": "`tab` — Layout",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/tab.png\" alt=\"tab\" width=\"720\">\n\nOne page of `tabs`, labelled by its title; pages share the card's state."
    },
    {
      "section": "`title` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/title.png\" alt=\"title\" width=\"720\">\n\nA headline line in five sizes."
    },
    {
      "section": "`text` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/text.png\" alt=\"text\" width=\"720\">\n\nA sentence, with `{…}` live values."
    },
    {
      "section": "`badge` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/badge.png\" alt=\"badge\" width=\"720\">\n\nA one-word status label in five tones."
    },
    {
      "section": "`callout` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/callout.png\" alt=\"callout\" width=\"720\">\n\nOne emphasized remark: an assumption, a caveat, a next step."
    },
    {
      "section": "`divider` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/divider.png\" alt=\"divider\" width=\"720\">\n\nA hairline separator."
    },
    {
      "section": "`link` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/link.png\" alt=\"link\" width=\"720\">\n\nA citation link, opened only when clicked."
    },
    {
      "section": "`image` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/image.png\" alt=\"image\" width=\"720\">\n\nAn inline `data:` image with alt text and a caption."
    },
    {
      "section": "`code` — Text",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/code.png\" alt=\"code\" width=\"720\">\n\nCode or other preformatted text, kept exactly as written, with syntax colours in the host's palette, line numbers, a copy button, and `current=` highlighting the running line."
    },
    {
      "section": "`metric` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/metric.png\" alt=\"metric\" width=\"720\">\n\nOne prominent number that recomputes as controls move."
    },
    {
      "section": "`progress` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/progress.png\" alt=\"progress\" width=\"720\">\n\nA proportion bar."
    },
    {
      "section": "`table` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/table.png\" alt=\"table\" width=\"720\">\n\nA comparison table; `current=` highlights a row, and `sortable=true` lets the reader sort by any column. Any table copies as CSV or Markdown; past 8 rows it gains a filter, and past 20 it pages."
    },
    {
      "section": "`keys` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/keys.png\" alt=\"keys\" width=\"720\">\n\nLabel and value pairs for exact figures."
    },
    {
      "section": "`list` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/list.png\" alt=\"list\" width=\"720\">\n\nA bulleted list; `current=` highlights an item."
    },
    {
      "section": "`steps` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/steps.png\" alt=\"steps\" width=\"720\">\n\nA numbered procedure; with `mono=true` and `current=`, a code listing with the running line highlighted."
    },
    {
      "section": "`chart` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/chart.png\" alt=\"chart\" width=\"720\">\n\nA bar, line, area, or pie chart of one `values=` series, or of up to four `series` lines."
    },
    {
      "section": "`series` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/series.png\" alt=\"series\" width=\"720\">\n\nOne named series of a chart, stacked or side by side; the legend hides and shows it, and a readout names one column's figures."
    },
    {
      "section": "`diagram` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/diagram.png\" alt=\"diagram\" width=\"720\">\n\nA flowchart laid out in layers; loops return along the side, and `current=` highlights a box."
    },
    {
      "section": "`canvas` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/canvas.png\" alt=\"canvas\" width=\"720\">\n\nA drawing: `shape` lines over an optional SVG, which is read into a checked tree. Pictured with one area clicked."
    },
    {
      "section": "`shape` — Data",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/shape.png\" alt=\"shape\" width=\"720\">\n\nOne thing on a canvas: a line, rectangle, circle, polygon, path, curve of a function, text, point, invisible area to click, or a part of the SVG placed by its id. Coordinates, turns, sizes, and fades are expressions, so a player animates them; a `point` with `drag=true` moves under the reader's pointer, and a click stores a value in a state."
    },
    {
      "section": "`plot` — Math",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/plot.png\" alt=\"plot\" width=\"720\">\n\nCurves of y = f(x) with a marked point, its tangent, and a shaded integral."
    },
    {
      "section": "`formula` — Math",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/formula.png\" alt=\"formula\" width=\"720\">\n\nA typeset expression with its live value."
    },
    {
      "section": "`slider` — Controls",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/slider.png\" alt=\"slider\" width=\"720\">\n\nA range slider bound to a number."
    },
    {
      "section": "`numberInput` — Controls",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/numberInput.png\" alt=\"numberInput\" width=\"720\">\n\nExact number entry."
    },
    {
      "section": "`textInput` — Controls",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/textInput.png\" alt=\"textInput\" width=\"720\">\n\nA one-line text field."
    },
    {
      "section": "`select` — Controls",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/select.png\" alt=\"select\" width=\"720\">\n\nA dropdown choice."
    },
    {
      "section": "`checkbox` — Controls",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/checkbox.png\" alt=\"checkbox\" width=\"720\">\n\nAn on/off switch."
    },
    {
      "section": "`checklist` — Controls",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/checklist.png\" alt=\"checklist\" width=\"720\">\n\nItems to tick off with a done count; `bind=` hands the count — or the sum of the ticked items' `values=` — to the rest of the card, and `names=` the ticked names."
    },
    {
      "section": "`button` — Action",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/button.png\" alt=\"button\" width=\"720\">\n\nSends its text as your next message, then locks the card."
    },
    {
      "section": "`player` — Animation",
      "text": "<img src=\"assets/catalog/player.png\" alt=\"player\" width=\"720\">\n\nA control bar at the bottom of the card: plays, pauses, steps, and scrubs a number at 0.5× to 2×; everything that reads it follows. `loop=true` repeats a run, and `autoplay=true` starts it while the card is on screen."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT License](LICENSE) © 2026 Starfield."
    }
  ],
